    "created_at": "2017-07-12T18:36:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-12T18:37:08Z",
    "body": "Difference between 2 and 3 is whether the 3D bits are preserved when you call getTransform().\r\n\r\nOption 3 is not great from an implementation stand point because it may require storing and maintaining an extra matrix representation under the hood (because the 2D readering lib may not support it). Plus you have to worry about how transforms (scale, rotate, etc.) apply to the 3D bits that we don't really care about.\r\n\r\nI am also happy with 1 or 2.  Leaning towards 2, which seems more developer friendly.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/314858707/reactions",
